-- Binding-layer satisfaction for anthill.geometry (proposal 038).
--
-- `VectorSpace requires Ring[F]`, and `Float`'s `provides Ring[Float]` is a per-language
-- binding claim (`float.anthill`) — so a stdlib-only load cannot satisfy this
-- provision, and it stands here rather than in `Vec3`'s own declaration. A
-- `namespace Vec3` SECONDARY ENTRY (059 R2/R3) is what gives it an address
-- without moving it; it was a namespace-level `fact VectorSpace[Vec3, Float]`
-- until WI-20260917-S8JYF retired that spelling (058 §4), and the positional
-- carrier it used to derive is now the entry's address.
--
-- The four members are BACKED: `anthill.geometry.Vec3` declares
-- `vec_add` / `vec_sub` / `vec_scale` / `vec_zero` as bodied operations.
-- A rule is not backing (WI-818), which is why the pre-WI-935 relational
-- `vec_add(?a, ?b, ?c)` clauses could not stand in for them.
namespace anthill.geometry
  import anthill.prelude.{Float}
  import anthill.prelude.algebra.{VectorSpace}

  namespace Vec3
    provides VectorSpace[V = Vec3, F = Float]
  end
end
